CORE
main.c
--no-simplify
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 11 member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 12 array member: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^Invariant check failed
--
Reading a member of a field-sensitive struct must yield the field itself even
when simplification is disabled. Else the back-end has to convert the struct
expression of all fields, which the incremental SMT back-end does not support
(it lacks conversion of the concatenation the struct is flattened to). A global
struct is used to avoid a declaration, which would otherwise also convert the
struct.
